  <notes>The left margin line numbers (5, 10, ... 50) are placed beside the verse lines where they stand; their exact line alignment is approximate. The woodcut initial P is joined to "ater" as "Pater". Doubtful readings: "Cœlumque" and "cœlo" may be printed with a ligature; the ligature is transcribed as œ. Two hyphenation marks: "rupi-mus" as printed. The verse lines are each given as one paragraph because the printed poem shows no clear stanza breaks.</notes>
